{"id":"mahabharata-12-008","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":8,"title":"अष्टमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 8 · Arjuna rebukes Yudhishthira","summary":{"en":"Arjuna, stung, answers that a man who has won a kingdom by the Kshatriya's dharma should not throw it away, and he cites the ancient ways of kings. He says that wealth is the means of dharma and that poverty is not holy.","kn":"ನೊಂದ ಅರ್ಜುನ ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯ ಧರ್ಮದಿಂದ ರಾಜ್ಯ ಗಳಿಸಿದವನು ಅದನ್ನು ಎಸೆಯಬಾರದೆಂದು ಉತ್ತರಿಸಿ ರಾಜರ ಹಳೆಯ ರೀತಿಗಳನ್ನು ಉಲ್ಲೇಖಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಧನವೇ ಧರ್ಮದ ಸಾಧನ, ದಾರಿದ್ರ್ಯ ಪವಿತ್ರವಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"आहत अर्जुन उत्तर देते हैं कि क्षत्रिय धर्म से राज्य जीतने वाले को उसे नहीं त्यागना चाहिए, और राजाओं की प्राचीन रीतियाँ बताते हैं। वे कहते हैं कि धन धर्म का साधन है और दरिद्रता पवित्र नहीं।","te":"నొచ్చుకున్న అర్జునుడు క్షత్రియ ధర్మంతో రాజ్యం గెలిచినవాడు దాన్ని వదలకూడదని బదులిచ్చి రాజుల పురాతన రీతులను పేర్కొంటాడు. ధనం ధర్మానికి సాధనమని, దారిద్ర్యం పవిత్రం కాదని అంటాడు.","ta":"புண்பட்ட அர்ஜுனன் க்ஷத்திரிய தர்மத்தால் நாட்டை வென்றவன் அதை விடக்கூடாது என்று பதிலளித்து மன்னரின் பழைய நெறிகளைக் கூறுகிறான். செல்வமே தர்மத்தின் கருவி, வறுமை புனிதமல்ல என்கிறான்.","ml":"ക്ഷുഭിതനായ അർജുനൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു: ക്ഷത്രിയധർമ്മത്തിലൂടെ രാജ്യം നേടിയവൻ അത് വലിച്ചെറിയരുത്; പുരാതന രാജമാർഗ്ഗങ്ങൾ അദ്ദേഹം ഉദ്ധരിക്കുന്നു. ധനം ധർമ്മത്തിന്റെ ഉപാധിയാണെന്നും ദാരിദ്ര്യം പുണ്യമല്ലെന്നും അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.8; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथार्जुन उवाचेदमधिक्षिप्त इवाक्षमी ।\nअभिनीततरं वाक्यं दृढवादपराक्रमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Arjuna, who could not bear the reproach, spoke these words, firm in speech and valor, and keenly pointed."}},{"n":2,"text":"दर्शयन्नैन्द्रिरात्मानमुग्रमुग्रपराक्रमः ।\nस्मयमानो महातेजाः सृक्किणी संलिहन्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Showing his fierce nature, the great-spirited son of Indra, terrible in prowess, smiled and repeatedly licked the corners of his mouth."}},{"n":3,"text":"अहो दुःखमहो कृच्छ्रमहो वैक्लव्यमुत्तमम् ।\nयत्कृत्वामानुषं कर्म त्यजेथाः श्रियमुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said: Ah, what sorrow, what hardship, what supreme weakness, that after doing superhuman deeds you would give up the greatest fortune!"}},{"n":4,"text":"शत्रून्हत्वा महीं लब्ध्वा स्वधर्मेणोपपादिताम् ।\nहतामित्रः कथं सर्वं त्यजेथा बुद्धिलाघवात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed your foes and won the earth by your own dharma, with your enemies slain, how can you give up everything through a failing of the mind?"}},{"n":5,"text":"क्लीबस्य हि कुतो राज्यं दीर्घसूत्रस्य वा पुनः ।\nकिमर्थं च महीपालानवधीः क्रोधमूर्छितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who is a eunuch in spirit or a procrastinator, where is a kingdom? Why then did you kill the kings, blind with anger?"}},{"n":6,"text":"यो ह्याजिजीविषेद्भैक्ष्यं कर्मणा नैव केनचित् ।\nसमारम्भान्बुभूषेत हतस्वस्तिरकिंचनः ।\nसर्वलोकेषु विख्यातो न पुत्रपशुसंहितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who would live by begging, without doing any work, who would give up all undertakings, his welfare lost, owning nothing, though famed in all worlds, and without sons or cattle,"}},{"n":7,"text":"कापालीं नृप पापिष्ठां वृत्तिमास्थाय जीवतः ।\nसंत्यज्य राज्यमृद्धं ते लोकोऽयं किं वदिष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, what will the world say of you, who would give up a flourishing kingdom and live by the sinful beggar's skull-bowl way?"}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्वारम्भान्समुत्सृज्य हतस्वस्तिरकिंचनः ।\nकस्मादाशंससे भैक्ष्यं चर्तुं प्राकृतवत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having cast aside every undertaking, your welfare lost and owning nothing, why do you wish, my lord, to go begging like a common man?"}},{"n":9,"text":"अस्मिन्राजकुले जातो जित्वा कृत्स्नां वसुंधराम् ।\nधर्मार्थावखिलौ हित्वा वनं मौढ्यात्प्रतिष्ठसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Born in this royal house, having conquered the whole earth, you are leaving both dharma and wealth entire, and in folly setting out for the forest."}},{"n":10,"text":"यदीमानि हवींषीह विमथिष्यन्त्यसाधवः ।\nभवता विप्रहीणानि प्राप्तं त्वामेव किल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If wicked men trample on these oblations here after you have left them, the guilt will surely fall on you."}},{"n":11,"text":"आकिंचन्यमनाशास्यमिति वै नहुषोऽब्रवीत् ।\nकृत्या नृशंसा ह्यधने धिगस्त्वधनतामिह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nahusha said that owning nothing is not to be wished for; for the poor, cruel magic arises. Shame on poverty in this world!"}},{"n":12,"text":"अश्वस्तनमृषीणां हि विद्यते वेद तद्भवान् ।\nयं त्विमं धर्ममित्याहुर्धनादेष प्रवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sages keep no store for tomorrow; you know that. But what is called dharma here proceeds from wealth."}},{"n":13,"text":"धर्मं संहरते तस्य धनं हरति यस्य यः ।\nह्रियमाणे धने राजन्वयं कस्य क्षमेमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever takes away a man's wealth takes away his dharma. When wealth is being taken away, O king, whom could we forgive?"}},{"n":14,"text":"अभिशस्तवत्प्रपश्यन्ति दरिद्रं पार्श्वतः स्थितम् ।\nदारिद्र्यं पातकं लोके कस्तच्छंसितुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"People look at a poor man standing beside them as if he were a cursed outcast. Poverty is a sin in the world; who can praise it?"}},{"n":15,"text":"पतितः शोच्यते राजन्निर्धनश्चापि शोच्यते ।\nविशेषं नाधिगच्छामि पतितस्याधनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"O king, a fallen man is pitied, and a poor man is pitied too; I see no difference between the fallen and the penniless."}},{"n":16,"text":"अर्थेभ्यो हि विवृद्धेभ्यः संभृतेभ्यस्ततस्ततः ।\nक्रियाः सर्वाः प्रवर्तन्ते पर्वतेभ्य इवापगाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From wealth that has grown, gathered from here and there, all undertakings flow, as rivers from mountains."}},{"n":17,"text":"अर्थाद्धर्मश्च कामश्च स्वर्गश्चैव नराधिप ।\nप्राणयात्रा हि लोकस्य विनार्थं न प्रसिध्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"From wealth come dharma, desire and heaven, O king; the world's livelihood cannot be achieved without wealth."}},{"n":18,"text":"अर्थेन हि विहीनस्य पुरुषस्याल्पमेधसः ।\nव्युच्छिद्यन्ते क्रियाः सर्वा ग्रीष्मे कुसरितो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"For a man without wealth and of small understanding, all undertakings dry up, like poor streams in summer."}},{"n":19,"text":"यस्यार्थास्तस्य मित्राणि यस्यार्थास्तस्य बान्धवाः ।\nयस्यार्थाः स पुमाँल्लोके यस्यार्थाः स च पण्डितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who has wealth has friends; he who has wealth has kin. He who has wealth is a man in this world; he who has wealth is a scholar."}},{"n":20,"text":"अधनेनार्थकामेन नार्थः शक्यो विवित्सता ।\nअर्थैरर्था निबध्यन्ते गजैरिव महागजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A poor man who wishes for wealth and tries to gain it cannot succeed; wealth is bound by wealth, as great elephants are caught by elephants."}},{"n":21,"text":"धर्मः कामश्च स्वर्गश्च हर्षः क्रोधः श्रुतं दमः ।\nअर्थादेतानि सर्वाणि प्रवर्तन्ते नराधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma, desire, heaven, joy, anger, learning and self-control, O king, all proceed from wealth."}},{"n":22,"text":"धनात्कुलं प्रभवति धनाद्धर्मः प्रवर्तते ।\nनाधनस्यास्त्ययं लोको न परः पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"From wealth a family arises and from wealth dharma goes forward. For the poor man there is neither this world nor the next, best of men."}},{"n":23,"text":"नाधनो धर्मकृत्यानि यथावदनुतिष्ठति ।\nधनाद्धि धर्मः स्रवति शैलाद्गिरिनदी यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"A poor man cannot properly carry out the rites of dharma; dharma flows from wealth as a mountain river flows from a rock."}},{"n":24,"text":"यः कृशाश्वः कृशगवः कृशभृत्यः कृशातिथिः ।\nस वै राजन्कृशो नाम न शरीरकृशः कृशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man whose horses are lean, whose cattle are lean, whose servants and guests are lean, is called lean, O king; not he whose body is lean."}},{"n":25,"text":"अवेक्षस्व यथान्यायं पश्य देवासुरं यथा ।\nराजन्किमन्यज्ज्ञातीनां वधादृध्यन्ति देवताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Consider this by right reasoning; look at the gods and the asuras. What else, king, but the killing of their kin made the gods prosper?"}},{"n":26,"text":"न चेद्धर्तव्यमन्यस्य कथं तद्धर्ममारभेत् ।\nएतावानेव वेदेषु निश्चयः कविभिः कृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If another's property were never to be taken, how could one begin any dharma? This much is the conclusion the sages reached in the Vedas."}},{"n":27,"text":"अध्येतव्या त्रयी विद्या भवितव्यं विपश्चिता ।\nसर्वथा धनमाहार्यं यष्टव्यं चापि यत्नतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The three Vedas must be studied and one must become learned; wealth must be gathered by every means, and sacrifices must be performed with effort."}},{"n":28,"text":"द्रोहाद्देवैरवाप्तानि दिवि स्थानानि सर्वशः ।\nइति देवा व्यवसिता वेदवादाश्च शाश्वताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By harming others the gods won their places in heaven, in every case. So the gods have determined, and so the eternal Vedic teachings say."}},{"n":29,"text":"अधीयन्ते तपस्यन्ति यजन्ते याजयन्ति च ।\nकृत्स्नं तदेव च श्रेयो यदप्याददतेऽन्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Men study, practice austerity, sacrifice and have sacrifices performed, and all that is good which they do even when they take from others."}},{"n":30,"text":"न पश्यामोऽनपहृतं धनं किंचित्क्वचिद्वयम् ।\nएवमेव हि राजानो जयन्ति पृथिवीमिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We see no wealth anywhere that was not taken from someone. Just so do kings conquer this earth."}},{"n":31,"text":"जित्वा ममत्वं ब्रुवते पुत्रा इव पितुर्धने ।\nराजर्षयो जितस्वर्गा धर्मो ह्येषां निगद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having conquered, they declare it theirs, as sons speak of a father's wealth. The royal sages who have won heaven say that this is their dharma."}},{"n":32,"text":"यथैव पूर्णादुदधेः स्यन्दन्त्यापो दिशो दश ।\nएवं राजकुलाद्वित्तं पृथिवीं प्रतितिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the waters flow to the ten directions from a full ocean, so wealth spreads over the earth from the royal house."}},{"n":33,"text":"आसीदियं दिलीपस्य नृगस्य नहुषस्य च ।\nअम्बरीषस्य मान्धातुः पृथिवी सा त्वयि स्थिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"This earth belonged to Dilipa, Nriga, Nahusha, Ambarisha and Mandhatri, and now it rests with you."}},{"n":34,"text":"स त्वां द्रव्यमयो यज्ञः संप्राप्तः सर्वदक्षिणः ।\nतं चेन्न यजसे राजन्प्राप्तस्त्वं देवकिल्बिषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A sacrifice made of material things, with every fee, has come to you. If you do not perform it, O king, you incur the guilt of the gods."}},{"n":35,"text":"येषां राजाश्वमेधेन यजते दक्षिणावता ।\nउपेत्य तस्यावभृथं पूताः सर्वे भवन्ति ते ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those for whom the king performs the horse sacrifice with generous fees become purified when they reach its closing bath."}},{"n":36,"text":"विश्वरूपो महादेवः सर्वमेधे महामखे ।\nजुहाव सर्वभूतानि तथैवात्मानमात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the great Sarvamedha sacrifice, Mahadeva, whose form is the universe, offered all beings and also himself, by himself."}},{"n":37,"text":"शाश्वतोऽयं भूतिपथो नास्यान्तमनुशुश्रुम ।\nमहान्दाशरथः पन्था मा राजन्कापथं गमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"This is the eternal path to prosperity, and we have not heard of any end to it. It is the great path of Dasharatha's son. King, do not take a wrong road."}}]}]}